    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The Uninhabited Aerial Vehicle Synthetic Aperture Radar (UAVSAR) is an airborne polarimetric radar instrument developed and operated by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL).\n\nUAVSAR provides differential interferometric measurements that help characterize deformation from phenomena such as earthquakes, volcanic activity, and glacial motion.\n\nThis dataset contains Repeat Pass Interferometric synthetic aperture radar products acquired by UAVSAR operating in the L-band frequency. Standard UAVSAR polarimetric synthetic aperture radar products can be found in the associated [UAVSAR  Polarimetric Synthetic Aperture Radar (PolSAR) Product] collection.",
